Output: 1 failed. Existing `search.txt` copied raw text, retaining blank lines and decomposed `café`; expected NFC-normalized tokens with single spaces. Test fixture uses the built-in PyMuPDF `japan` font because base Helvetica substitutes combining acute with middle dot; raw expected includes the extractor's actual two-space gap. This confirms the RED behavior before implementation.
GREEN — implementation and regressions
Implementation: digitization/native.py now records the exact PyMuPDF page text (adding a terminal LF only when needed to delimit page text), tokenizes that raw text by Unicode whitespace, aligns every PyMuPDF word in order using NFC equality, and raises on any unaligned/missing token. `search.txt` is NFC-normalized extractor words joined by one ASCII space; each word carries independent half-open raw and search offsets, raw text, source word box, transformed page box and frame. `page-map.json` records cropbox, rotation, named source/target frames and the PyMuPDF rotation matrix. Inspection verifies artifacts, extraction configuration/options, complete normalized search text, offsets, boxes/transforms and line/page frame relationships. The baseline native test now expects single-space normalized search while retaining its raw text, word/span, geometry, descriptor, integrity and fresh-process assertions.
Focused RED after feature implementation exposed two adjustments: raw text needs an LF boundary where an extracted page lacks one (preserves the prior two-page raw contract); and the built-in font's wide two-space gap caused PyMuPDF to return distinct layout groups, which the new test now pins as extractor grouping. These were corrected without altering layout semantics.
